Testing Execution Order

1. Smoke Testing (Build Verification Testing)
✅ First thing you do after getting a new build
🎯 Purpose: Check if the build is stable enough for testing
🔍 Covers: Critical functionalities only (login, app launch, basic navigation)

👉 If Smoke fails → Reject the build ❌

2. Sanity Testing
✅ Done after smoke passes OR after minor changes / bug fixes
🎯 Purpose: Verify specific functionality is working fine
🔍 Focused & narrow testing (not full coverage)

👉 If Sanity fails → Send back for fix ❌

3. Regression Testing
✅ After sanity passes and build is stable
🎯 Purpose: Ensure existing features are not broken
🔍 Covers previously tested modules

👉 Usually automated using Selenium/TestNG

4. Functional Testing
🎯 Purpose: Validate all features against requirements (SRS/BRD)
🔍 Includes:
UI testing
API testing
Integration testing

5. System Testing
🎯 Purpose: Test the entire application as a whole
🔍 End-to-end scenarios

6. User Acceptance Testing (UAT)
🎯 Done by client/business users
🔍 Validates if system meets business needs

7. Ad-hoc / Exploratory Testing
🎯 Random testing to find unexpected bugs
🔍 No predefined test cases

8. Retesting
🎯 Verify fixed defects
🔁 Done after bug fixes

